{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe six workflow files below contain repeated, obvious, historical, or stale prose identified by the comment audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `c019920390926d543a0813d4c0c8721543d98776`. Shortening it must preserve trigger, permission, security, and evidence contracts.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only standalone comments and blank lines in the declared files. Preserve workflow data and behavior-bearing scanner directives byte-for-byte. Replace narration with the minimum current rationale needed by each consumer.\n\n## Scope\n- `reconcile-bridge.yml` — Preserve copyable-client semantics; hourly/manual modes; Actions and ref-lock concurrency; full-history tickets worktree with merge-not-rebase/merge driver; job-local permissions; completed-pass-only 60-minute ceiling; pinned acli; temporary signing key/unsigned fallback; fail-loud no-op detection; default-off paced continuous chain with bounded failure handling; and conditional dimensionless CloudWatch metrics that never alter job outcome. Consumers: client Actions, Jira/tickets, ref-lock, heartbeat canary, CloudWatch.\n- `release.yml` — Preserve dispatch-from-main authorization; version/registry/ancestry/environment/advisory guards; immutable pins; build-once artifacts with digest and baked-commit provenance; installed wheel/sdist tests; exact-byte OIDC PyPI promotion; post-publish tag/release; unprivileged publisher-digest verification before OIDC use; bounded idempotent registry publish; evidence fragments; two `# shellcheck disable=SC1091` directives; and `# zizmor:ignore[excessive-permissions]`. Consumers: release operators, PyPI, MCP Registry, GitHub Releases and supply-chain evidence.\n- `structured-output-baseline.yml` — Preserve manual canonical-repository billable measurement; pre-call budget refusal; independent provider arms and secrets; Bedrock OIDC with both regions and step-confined exchange; external-test opt-in; provider overlays; 3600-second whole-sweep timeout; and always-uploaded unique raw results. Consumer: evaluation operators and structured-matrix tests.\n- `terraform-drift.yml` — Preserve Terraform-path PRs plus daily/manual runs (no push); independent fmt/plan jobs; plan-only OIDC; full-history checkout and current-tree assertion with accepted checkout/fetch race; Terraform 1.11.4 floor; validate-before-plan; detailed exit codes with `-lock=false`; advisory role outside Gerrit Verified; and exact `# mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker. Consumers: Actions/Terraform operators, OIDC role and tree-currency check.\n- `test.yml` — Preserve ordinary pushes excluding `feature/**`, `main`, and `tickets`; all PRs; six-hour/manual health; same-ref cancellation; shared Gerrit workflows; schedule-only mutation omission; clean-install path; soft last-green/bisect report; actual external self-skip behavior when manually enabled without credentials; breadth-tier blocking/advisory distinctions; nonblocking external link check; and exact `# predates-gate-ok:` marker. Do not claim every trigger runs the full suite.\n- `verify-identity.yml` — Preserve config-driven advisory authentication policy and grandfathering; triggers/exclusions; full-history blobless checkout; temporary fail-closed pack limit with explicit restoration; tickets worktree; ancestry-based key verification; object-database immutability; and config-driven op-cert verification without CI overrides. Do not claim current merge-gate enforcement or absence of signatures.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only standalone comments or blank lines in the six declared files; behavior-bearing directives remain exact.\n- [ ] Every Scope constraint and consumer contract has a PASS row with concrete before/after citations in a leaf-linked session log authored by a reviewer who did not write the remediation.\n- [ ] Every edited comment block has an independent `bloat-removal` PASS row confirming that redundant, obvious, duplicated, historical, or stale prose was removed while current non-obvious rationale remained.\n- [ ] Focused workflow tests, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and repository lint pass at the leaf commit.\n- [ ] No missing or FAIL semantic-preservation row remains at closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded comment-only guard, focused workflow suites, path-scoped diff check, and worktree-venv lint."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788597649994944001,"uuid":"823c9394-369a-4d8d-8ab7-fc62957f0025"}